<title>HONG KONG: Harbin Power 1996 net down 30.7 percent.</title>
<headline>Harbin Power 1996 net down 30.7 percent.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31</p>
<p>(in million yuan unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (yuan)		   0.071    vs  0.103</p>
<p>    Dividend (yuan)	    0.035    vs  0.035</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  nil	vs  nil</p>
<p>    Net			    84.53    vs  122.09</p>
<p>    Turnover		     2,402.82 vs  2,667.98</p>
<p>    Company name		 Harbin Power Equipment Co Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  May 28 to June 27</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   August 29</p>
<p>NOTE - Harbin Power is China's largest power equipment maker.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is 0.035 yuan vs 0.05 yuan.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
